Round 3's report opened a plain ``` fence and, inside it, a ```diff fence at
line 559. CommonMark closes a fence only on a backtick run with no info
string, so to a strict reader line 559 is content; to a reader that treats
every fence-looking line as a boundary it is a boundary. The pairings differ
by one from there on, and `## Tests added` (line 655), `## Gates`,
`## Invariants touched` and `## Known gaps / follow-ups` end up inside a code
block for the second reader — invisible to the scanner that reported the
gap. The inherited edit removes the nested ```diff fences; both readings now
pair the same regions. It is pinned by `tests/report_markdown_test.rs`, which
fails on the old shape and on an unterminated fence, and accepts a balanced
document.

